    s: `For equations like {{x + y = 4}} and {{x − y = 2}}, put the coefficients in a matrix A and the right-hand sides in b, then {{np.linalg.solve(A, b)}} returns the solution — prefer it to computing the inverse. {{np.linalg.det}} and {{np.linalg.inv}} are there too, but {{solve}} is faster and more accurate.`,
